---
const problems = [
  {
    icon: `<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 3h5v5"/><path d="M4 20L21 3"/><path d="M21 16v5h-5"/><path d="M15 15l6 6"/><path d="M4 4l5 5"/></svg>`,
    title: 'Fragmented Transports',
    desc: 'MCP stdio, HTTP, REST, CLI - each requires a different server setup, different libraries, different patterns.'
  },
  {
    icon: `<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 01-2-2V4a2 2 0 012-2h9a2 2 0 012 2v1"/></svg>`,
    title: 'Boilerplate Overload',
    desc: 'Every new endpoint means repeating validation, error handling, and serialization. Your business logic drowns in glue code.'
  },
  {
    icon: `<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg>`,
    title: 'Framework Lock-in',
    desc: 'Pick Express? Now you\'re stuck. Pick Fastify? Same story. Your actions are trapped inside your transport choice.'
  }
]
---

<section class="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">The Problem</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Agents need services. Services need many doors.</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      The agentic landscape demands that services be reachable via MCP, REST, CLI, and more.
      Building each transport from scratch is unsustainable.
    </p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      {problems.map(p => (
        <div class="problem-card">
          <div class="problem-icon" set:html={p.icon} />
          <h3>{p.title}</h3>
          <p>{p.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .problem-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .problem-card {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .problem-icon {
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .problem-card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .problem-card p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .problem-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
